---
// Fig. for "Linear Algebra over Finite Fields": vectors add and scale
// entry-by-entry mod 7, and the dot product (2,3,5)·(4,1,6) = 41 = 6
// collapses two lists into one number.
---
<svg viewBox="0 0 760 500" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block;">
  <text x="380" y="26" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="16" font-weight="800" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">vectors and the dot product</text>

  <rect x="40" y="46" width="680" height="42" rx="10" fill="#111c2e" stroke="#3ab7ff" stroke-width="1.5" />
  <text x="380" y="72" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8fdcff" font-size="13.5" font-weight="700" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">What can we do with lists of numbers mod 7?</text>

  <text x="380" y="118" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8b96a8" font-size="12" font-weight="700" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">STEP 1 &#8212; add and scale, entry by entry</text>
  <text x="380" y="146" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="14.5" font-weight="700" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">(2, 3, 5) + (4, 1, 6) = (6, 4, 11) = (6, 4, 4)</text>
  <text x="380" y="176" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="14.5" font-weight="700" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">3 &#215; (2, 3, 5) = (6, 9, 15) = (6, 2, 1)</text>
  <text x="380" y="202" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8b96a8" font-size="11.5" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">11 &#8722; 7 = 4, 9 &#8722; 7 = 2, 15 &#8722; 14 = 1</text>

  <text x="380" y="246" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8b96a8" font-size="12" font-weight="700" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">STEP 2 &#8212; the dot product</text>
  <text x="380" y="274" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="15" font-weight="700" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">(2, 3, 5) &#8226; (4, 1, 6) = 2&#215;4 + 3&#215;1 + 5&#215;6 = 8 + 3 + 30 = 41</text>
  <text x="380" y="300" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5ddc8a" font-size="13.5" font-weight="700" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">41 = 5 &#215; 7 + 6 = 6</text>

  <rect x="260" y="322" width="240" height="42" rx="10" fill="#0e1f16" stroke="#5ddc8a" stroke-width="1.8" />
  <text x="380" y="348" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5ddc8a" font-size="13.5" font-weight="700" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">a dot product gives one number</text>

  <text x="380" y="396" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="13" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">reduce first: 8 = 1 and 30 = 2, so 1 + 3 + 2 = 6 &#10003;</text>

  <line x1="40" y1="416" x2="720" y2="416" stroke="#223049" stroke-width="1" />
  <text x="380" y="440" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8fdcff" font-size="15.5" font-weight="800" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">TWO LISTS IN, ONE NUMBER OUT</text>
  <text x="380" y="462" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8b96a8" font-size="12.5" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">Every step is ordinary arithmetic, then reduce mod 7.</text>
</svg>
